\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab GLORIOUS things of thee are spoken,
\par \pard\li720 Zion, city of our God ;
\par He, whose word cannot be broken,
\par Formed thee for His own abode.
\par On the Rock of Ages founded,
\par What can shake thy sure repose ?
\par With salvation's walls surrounded,
\par Thou may'st smile at all thy foes.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab See, the streams of living waters,
\par \pard\fi360\li360 Springing from eternal love,
\par Well supply thy sons and daughters,
\par And all fear of want remove:
\par \pard\li720 Who can faint, while such a river 
\par Ever flows their thirst to assuage ?
\par Grace which, like the Lord, the Giver,
\par Never fails from age to age.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab Saviour, if of Zion's city
\par \pard\fi360\li360 I, through grace, a member am,
\par Let the world deride or pity,
\par I will glory in Thy name :
\par Fading is the worldling's pleasure,
\par All his boasted pomp and show ;
\par Solid joys and lasting treasure
\par None but Zion's children know. 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

